    "id": "pediatric-echo-buying-guide",
    "key": "pediatric-echo",
    "kind": "research-guide",
    "equipmentId": null,
    "title": "Pediatric echo: an adult cardiac package may leave a gap",
    "summary": "Compare the exact probes and analysis for the children and neonatal work the service will cover. A pediatric preset is not a complete package.",
    "categoryId": "imaging",
    "category": "Imaging & radiology",
    "minutes": 3,
    "sections": [
      [
        "Define the patient range before comparing machines",
        "A service caring for older children may have a different equipment brief from one covering neonatal or complex congenital work. Have the pediatric echo lead define the population, examinations, measurements and reviewing workflow. Do not carry an adult purchasing specification across unchanged or assume that every cardiac system listed by a reseller provides the same pediatric capability. ASE’s 2024 pediatric TTE overview addresses traditional and adjunct imaging modalities as well as organizational and quality matters. It reinforces the need for a service-specific brief. The clinical team should determine which functions are necessary; procurement should establish that those functions are supplied, usable and supportable."
      ],
      [
        "A documented probe distinction is more useful than a preset name",
        "In Philips’ July 2016 CX50 xMATRIX table, S8-3 is identified for pediatric 2D echo and S12-4 for neonatal 2D echo, separately from the adult S5-1. GE’s historical Vivid iq page identifies 6S-RS and 12S-RS in its pediatric section. These are exact configuration leads, not proof that any used unit with the same console name includes them. Keep suffixes, console release and licensed analysis together in the comparison. Similar probe names do not establish interchangeability. Obtain current compatibility documentation for the proposed package, then have qualified users evaluate it for the intended patient range. An adult demonstration cannot settle that acceptance decision."
      ],
      [
        "Compare a shared platform with a complete dedicated service",
        "Adding the right supported probe to an existing adult platform can preserve training, reporting and service arrangements. That can be an economical first comparison when the platform is otherwise suitable. Include any required analysis, ECG accessories and software rights; price the actual addition rather than assuming the probe alone completes it. A dedicated system earns its place when sharing prevents timely access or the installed platform cannot supply an accepted pediatric package. Examine the schedule: who needs the scanner, in which location, and what happens when adult and pediatric demands coincide? A second console solves a scheduling problem only if the necessary probes and qualified staff are also available."
      ],
      [
        "Make the demonstration reach the reviewing clinician",
        "Use the responsible team’s approved evaluation arrangements to assess the defined work on the exact configuration. Follow acquisition into measurements, saved studies and the report received by the interpreting clinician. Record any task that depends on an absent option or separate workstation. The buyer needs the result of the evaluation, not an instruction to reproduce clinical examinations from a sales guide. Assess how the equipment will reach and fit the actual care area, with the needed accessories stored and protected. Include cleaning and charging arrangements, the availability of an appropriate cart and the staff handover between users. A compact specification is useful only if it makes the intended service easier to deliver."
      ],
      [
        "Budget for the pediatric probe that stops the service",
        "Separate the probe’s condition and repair route from the console’s. A provider able to repair the scanner may have no compatible temporary pediatric probe. Establish the actual substitute or alternative service before counting a loaner promise as cover. If one probe is indispensable, its replacement cost and access can matter more than a modest console discount. Keep the installed platform when a complete supported addition passes the defined evaluation and access is adequate. Choose a dedicated or different system when it closes a demonstrated population, function or scheduling gap. Neither brochure provides a measured reliability ranking or current price comparison, so those claims should not decide the shortlist."
      ]
    ],
