    "id": "breast-ultrasound-buying-guide",
    "key": "breast-ultrasound",
    "kind": "research-guide",
    "equipmentId": null,
    "title": "Breast ultrasound: make the probe package earn the upgrade",
    "summary": "Compare the required imaging, reporting and approved procedure setup before paying for elastography or AI. Exact probes and enabled options matter more than a premium model badge.",
    "categoryId": "imaging",
    "category": "Imaging & radiology",
    "minutes": 3,
    "sections": [
      [
        "Choose the service before the feature list",
        "An established breast-imaging team should define what the ultrasound package must do: required diagnostic imaging, documentation and any planned image-guided work. Keep this equipment decision distinct from the wider screening or mammography pathway. The buyer’s job is to fund the agreed service, not infer a clinical protocol from a product brochure. Separate essential functions from desirable additions. If the current accepted system completes the required work but its probe needs replacement, compare that repair or replacement first. A new console earns its place when it closes a defined imaging, workflow, access or support gap that a smaller investment cannot solve."
      ],
      [
        "Compare exact probe and platform combinations",
        "Philips illustrates breast imaging with EPIQ Elite and eL18-4. Its eL18-4 specification page lists breast use and identifies biopsy and image-fusion navigation capability. These are useful configuration leads, but “capable” does not mean the offered package includes every required accessory or software option. GE’s LOGIQ E10 materials show breast imaging and 2D shear-wave examples with ML4-20-D. That gives a second named combination to investigate. Neither manufacturer’s selected images establish a head-to-head winner, and a quote for an EPIQ Elite or LOGIQ E10 without the exact probe and enabled functions is not yet a comparable offer."
      ],
      [
        "Make elastography and AI separate buying decisions",
        "An advanced tool should have a named purpose in the clinical brief and an agreed way to evaluate it. Establish which function is required, where it runs, whether its licence transfers, and whether additional reporting or workstation software is needed. Otherwise an attractive option can consume money needed for the everyday probe, service or staffing. Check regional availability and the exact software release rather than assuming that everything on a manufacturer’s application page is available on the offered machine. Philips’ breast page carries an availability limitation, so a buyer should obtain clear product-specific evidence for any proposed AI feature. Do not price an advertised future capability as an included present benefit."
      ],
      [
        "A biopsy-capable probe is not a complete procedure package",
        "For planned image-guided work, have qualified staff identify the approved probe/accessory combination and the required supplies and processing route. Reconcile the bracket, guide or other necessary components against the offer. A generic biopsy-capable field cannot establish that a particular accessory fits or that it is included. Evaluate handling and the actual clinical workflow through the team’s approved acceptance process. Account for preparation, inspection, cleaning, storage and availability between cases. A second accepted probe may solve an availability problem more directly than another imaging option; its ongoing care and support still belong in the comparison."
      ],
      [
        "Follow the examination into the record",
        "Demonstrate the required labels, annotations, measurements, saved images and report using the offered configuration. Establish what transfers into the receiving system and what must be entered again. A good image shown at the console is only one part of a complete diagnostic workflow. Finally compare probe repair or replacement, temporary cover and the limits of the actual warranty. Do not turn a reseller’s broad warranty promise into assumed coverage for every transducer or destination. The better purchase is the accepted package that meets the service’s requirements at a supportable total cost, with optional functions priced for the value they actually add."
      ]
    ],
