        "Keep an accepted route until the new one is ready",
        "Arrange the cutover in stages: resolve compatibility, confirm the actual site and service scope, install and qualify, train staff and prove the records/release workflow, then transfer the accepted workload. Preserve backup capacity for devices or loads still awaiting resolution. A delivery date is not a clinical release date. The hospital-specific choice remains conditional on its instrument inventory and qualified acceptance. Public descriptions can establish meaningful capability differences, but they do not establish an installed price, local uptime or a universal brand winner. Keep a serviceable system when its whole-service case remains stronger; change it when the documented benefit survives the complete transition."
